From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:08:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 47/76] ci: run every workflow on the self-hosted
 hough-labs-k3s runner (gcp-3d7n)

All five workflow files targeted Blacksmith's hosted runners -- six `runs-on`
lines of billed cloud compute (ci 1, codeql 1, gascity-pack-inference 1,
pack-release-compatibility 1, supported-pack-nightly 2). The standing
requirement is that this pipeline runs on the Overseer's own hardware on anvil,
precisely so it does not depend on metered cloud minutes. `hough-labs-k3s` is
the org-wide label for that runner, and gascity-packs was the sole repo still
pointing elsewhere: gauntlet, pelican, mill, kindling and ember all target it
across their ci/release/security workflows.

The urgency is the three scheduled workflows. codeql, pack-release-compatibility
and supported-pack-nightly are currently state=disabled_fork (GitHub disables
crons on forks) and are slated to be re-enabled on anvil. Had they been armed
while still carrying a cloud label, three crons would have begun firing at a
runner that does not resolve, accumulating permanently-queued runs -- the
failure was already demonstrated live by run 33199131342, which queued on
["blacksmith-32vcpu-ubuntu-2404"] and had to be cancelled. Converting all five
is therefore the precondition for arming the nightlies, not a tidy-up.

The workflow diff is the six `runs-on` lines and nothing else: no job renamed,
no step added, removed or reordered, and no `on:`/`branches:`/`schedule:` key
touched (trigger scoping belongs to gcp-75ed, not here). Two judgement calls are
recorded deliberately rather than assumed. First, supported-pack-nightly sizes
its two jobs differently upstream (2vcpu and 32vcpu); anvil is a single
repurposed box exposing one label, not a sized fleet, so both collapse onto
`hough-labs-k3s` -- no size-suffixed label was invented, since that is the only
label verified live in this org. Second, no toolchain bootstrap step was added
anywhere, because none is needed: each workflow already drives
`actions/setup-go` / `actions/setup-python` before any `go install` or
`pip install`, which is exactly how the sibling repos run on this same label
with no extra setup (pelican drives setup-python; mill, kindling and gauntlet
drive setup-go).

The label swap regressed a test, which is the non-obvious part of this commit.
`tests/test_gascity_pack_inference_gate.py` pinned the blacksmith labels in
three places. That gate is upstream-correct -- upstream runs on Blacksmith
deliberately, as a project sponsor -- but fork-wrong, so it is updated rather
than deleted, and deliberately strengthened rather than merely inverted. It now
asserts per file that every `runs-on:` is the self-hosted label with no mixed
targets, then sweeps the whole workflow directory so that any file, including
one added later, fails here if it carries `blacksmith` or a GitHub-hosted
fallback. That converts a per-file allowlist into a real drift guard, so the
next billed-label workflow is caught in review rather than at 3am. The
README/Blacksmith sponsor-badge test is untouched: sponsorship is a separate
matter from where jobs execute. The gate is renamed to
test_ci_workflows_use_self_hosted_runner_labels; the old name had no other
references.

Validation: all five workflows re-parse as YAML; `git diff origin/integration --
.github/` is exactly the six runs-on lines; post-change per-file `runs-on`
counts are 1,1,1,1,2, all `hough-labs-k3s`, and `grep -r blacksmith .github/` is
empty. `make check-patches` exits 0. Full pack pytest suite 813 passed / 3
failed, and those 3 (test_no_bare_bd_commands, two test_formula_assets claim
cases) fail identically on unmodified origin/integration -- confirmed in a
scratch worktree, so they are pre-existing and unrelated. Also green: go vet,
go build, go test -race, and validate_registry.py --require-git.

One assumption stays unverified by design, per the bead's caveat: whether the
org runner group admits this fork needs admin:org to read. If the first run
after gcp-399 sits queued on "waiting for a runner", the fix is a runner-group
access change, NOT a revert to a cloud label -- that would silently reintroduce
the billed-minutes dependency this commit removes. Sibling defects gcp-399 (CI
never registers on this fork) and gcp-75ed (ci.yml scoped `branches: [main]`)
remain open and are not folded in here.
